A||||9||SCCA FIERO||Fiero won't pass emessions
Z||000000||SCCA FIERO||06-15-99||06:40 PM||||My 88 coupe won't pass emissions. I replaced the plugs,wires,filters and changed the oil. It got better ,but not good enough. What else could it be? My check engine light has never come on so I don't think it's a sensor. The light comes on at start up so I know it works. <p>The Hydrocarbons are not passing. The first test i had a reading of 411ppm at idle I have to have less than 220ppm to pass. I had 26ppm at high rpms and passed there.<p>The second test i had 364ppm at idle and 78 ppm at high speed. Again I have to be below 220ppm on both. The high speed is no problem,but at idle it just won't pass. Why?
Z||000001||Gokart||06-15-99||08:16 PM||||Check the exhaust system for any holes/leaks and/or possible replacement! Good luck!
Z||000002||ezsurf||06-15-99||09:26 PM||||If your not running the correct temperature thermostat this will effect your emissions.  Also, it depends on what mods you've done to the engine (if any).  Do you still have your EGR tube hooked up?  Is the engine timing set right for the tpye of fuel your running? There are a number of things to check. You have already knocked out several. Just add to the grocery list and continue to eliminate them one at a time.
Z||000003||SCCA FIERO||06-15-99||09:43 PM||||Gokart, will an exhaust leak cause it to fail?                                              <br>Ezsurf,I just bought the car about a week ago. It had a cracked exhaust manifold,but I fixed that. This car uses coil packs. Can the timing be set on the 88 4 cylinders? I'm not sure about the thermostat. 
Z||000004||theogre||06-16-99||12:34 AM||||1. a catalyst that is bad, or not hot enough, will often fail it. make sure you run the motor at no less than 1200 rpm for 45-90 seconds prior to pulling up to the emmisions test. (Delaware flat tells you that prior to pulling into the lanes.)<p>2. the rest of the engine of course has to also be in the proper temp range.<p>3. 1 or more injectors not sealing fully will cause rich mix.<p>4. the ECM may have an error in it and you just don't know it. check, and clear, any codes. an ECM in open loop mode will run rich allot of the time.<p>5. a bad vapor canistor can cause rich mix.<p>
Z||000005||lowCG||06-17-99||01:19 AM||||I've used high octane(very high,racing)gas to help this.I don't know if you're lucky and have access to testing equipment like I do to expirement with,but a dose of alcohol can also help.I would only do this with a low tank of gas so you can fill the tank again right away after your test,as alcohol can be harmful to certain(expensive)parts of the fuel system with regular,continous use.I've used naptha as an octane booster before as well,never tried it with emission testing however.To make sure and set your timing to the most retarded side of the tolerance should help also.Good luck.
Z||000006||terryk||08-06-99||12:07 AM||||Replace the cat. If the cat is new and they don't check the timing, run it at TDC.<p>In California, the idle test is after the high rpm test so the cat is cooking for the idle test.<p>We've made emission chips some emission chips too.
Z||000007||ChadMan||08-06-99||07:27 AM||||You can't set the timing on the 88 Coupes.  There's not even a timing mark!
Z||000008||86_Fastback||08-06-99||11:20 AM||||The next thing I would do is replace the oxygen sensor.  As the sensor ages, it gets lazy and doesn't react to changes very fast.  If replacing the oxygen sensor doesn't work, I would lean towards the cat even though it seems fine at higher rpms.<br>-Gregg
Z||000009||SCCA FIERO||08-06-99||12:49 PM||||This thread is kinda old. BNBoomer has the motor in question now. I repalced this 4 cylinder in my 88 coupe with a 2.8 V6. When I took the exhaust assembly out everything that is supposed to be in the cat ran down the pipes. That's my guess, the cat was FUBAR.
